WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.259 --> 00:00:08.660
Nothing symbolizes democratic government more
than the vote.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:13.010
Behind me is the polling place where I vote
on Election Day.

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:17.870
On Election Day, there's a long line outside
the door.

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:20.230
Election Day is the last day of the campaign.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:25.170
In the case of the United States, it's the
last day of a very long campaign.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:27.410
We have a marathon campaign.

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:29.390
That's different than European campaigns.

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:31.000
They last a few weeks.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.620
In the United States, they last for months
and months.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:37.930
One reason for that is that we have primary
elections.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:40.460
Candidates have to run first in the primary.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:43.550
And if they win, then they run in the general
election.

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:46.350
European democracies do not have primaries.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:49.699
American campaigns differ also in other ways.

00:00:49.699 --> 00:00:53.920
If you're watching an American campaign on
television, you'll see lots and lots of televised

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.420
political ads.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:59.839
Some democracies prohibit or ban the use of
televised ads.

00:00:59.839 --> 00:01:03.789
Others restrict the time period in which they
can be shown.

00:01:03.789 --> 00:01:09.210
Another way in which American elections differ
is that they are a lot more expensive.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:13.670
Federal campaign now in the United States
will cost more than a billion dollars that's

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:19.400
20 times what a campaign would cost in Germany
or Britain or Spain.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:24.110
Make no mistake, there is an American way
of conducting elections.

